Day 10 of 90 with @MyFirstHack 🔐

Today was about data — the thing every breach is really about, underneath all the technical details.

I learned to classify data into three categories: **PII, credentials, and proprietary data.** I also explored where personal information can live across everyday digital services.

I opened Google Takeout and selected four services: Chrome, Gmail, YouTube, and Drive. I haven't explored the exported data yet, and while checking the services I use, I haven't noticed anything surprising so far.

One category I hadn't thought deeply about before today was **browsing activity** — the information trail that can build up through everyday use of a browser.

Ten days in. The lens is starting to feel like a habit.

**80 days left.** 🔍

